{
  "id": 445965281,
  "iid": 23191,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Qt: Don't compute the scroll minimap while packet list is frozen",
  "description": "Dissecting packets in order to determine the proper colors for the\nscrollbar minimap is a waste of time when the packet list is frozen.\n\nIf the PacketList model is a nullptr, i.e. the packet list is frozen,\nthe scrollbar isn't being displayed. Also we are likely in the middle\nof changing profiles, where preferences have been reset to their\ndefault values but the new values might not have been applied, so\nthe dissection and thus the colors computed might not be accurate.\nThey are invalidated when the redissection with the new preferences\nfinishes anyway.\n\nRelated to #20903",
